.TH NR 1 "August 2026" "nr 0.3.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nr \- Git-aware NixOS lifecycle helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nr
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nr
builds, previews, activates, updates, checks, and publishes a NixOS flake.
Lifecycle commands build through
.BR nixos-rebuild (8),
parse Nix internal JSON events directly, show a bounded derivation dependency
graph, explain closure and activation impact, and preserve the backend exit
code.
.PP
The full backend stream is captured in a log file. Terminal output is intended
to answer what is changing, what is currently building or fetching, what
activation would do, and how to recover.
.PP
The rich rebuild graph is built from derivation edges loaded with
.BR "nix-store --query --graph" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Build the selected host without activating it. By default, leaves a
.B result
link in the current working directory.
.TP
.B switch
Build, show the closure diff, dry-activate, then activate the new system.
.TP
.B test
Build and activate until the next reboot. The boot default remains unchanged.
.TP
.B boot
Build and register the new generation as the next boot default without
activating it immediately.
.TP
.B preview
Build into a temporary directory, show the closure diff, and dry-activate
without mutating bootloader or profile state.
.TP
.B apply
Activate a saved preview plan without rebuilding.
.TP
.B rollback
Show the generation being rolled back to, then roll back. Without an argument,
runs the official previous-generation rollback:
.BR "nixos-rebuild switch --rollback" .
With a generation number or pin label, activates that generation store path.
.TP
.B generations
Show NixOS generations, annotated with any
.B nr pin
labels.
.TP
.B diff
Diff the current system against a path, generation, or flake. If no
.B --to
is provided, builds the selected flake in a temporary directory and diffs
against it.
.TP
.B gc
Run
.BR nix-collect-garbage (1)
with safer defaults. By default, deletes generations older than
.BR 7d .
.TP
.B pin
Label a NixOS generation in
.BR "$XDG_STATE_HOME/nr/pins.toml" .
.TP
.B unpin
Remove a generation pin and its GC root.
.TP
.B pins
List pinned generations and optionally report stale pin metadata.
.TP
.B history
Show bounded switch, test, and boot history.
.TP
.B logs
List retained logs and reports, or print the latest failed log path.
.TP
.B show-report
Print a retained lifecycle report.
.TP
.B inputs
Inspect flake inputs or update selected inputs.
.TP
.B init-config
Create a starter repository
.B nr
configuration file. Use
.B --user
to write the starter user config at
.BR ~/.config/nr/config.toml .
.TP
.B completions
Generate shell completions.
.TP
.B update
Update
.B flake.lock
or selected flake inputs. With
.BR --switch ,
perform Git preflight before updating, then build and activate.
.TP
.B publish
Review changes, commit them, and optionally push.
.TP
.B check
Run configured checks. The default is
.BR "nix flake check" .
.TP
.B doctor
Show target, config, dependency, and Git diagnostics.
.TP
.B cheat
Print a compact terminal reference.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--flake " PATH[#HOST]
Select the flake path and optionally the host.
.TP
.BI "--host " HOST
Override the NixOS configuration name.
.TP
.BI "--ui " auto|rich|nom|plain|raw|json|jsonl
Select output mode. The default,
.BR auto ,
uses
.B nom
for interactive lifecycle builds and plain output otherwise.
.TP
.BI "--log-file " PATH
Capture the full backend log at
.IR PATH .
Without this flag, logs are written under
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/nr/logs/
or
.BR ~/.local/state/nr/logs/ .
.TP
.B --dry
Alias lifecycle commands to preview-style behavior.
.TP
.B --ask
Ask before activation.
.TP
.B --offline
Forward offline mode to Nix.
.TP
.B --show-trace
Forward Nix traces.
.TP
.BI "--elevate " none|sudo|run0
Forward the
.BR nixos-rebuild (8)
privilege-elevation method used by dry activation, activation, and rollback.
.TP
.B --ask-elevate-password
Prompt locally and pipe an elevation password to
.BR nixos-rebuild .
Interactive non-root
.BR switch ,
.BR test ,
.BR boot ,
and
.B rollback
use
.B --elevate sudo
by default, so sudo normally owns the password prompt. This flag is mainly for
remote or non-TTY elevation flows.
.TP
.B --notify
Send a desktop notification when lifecycle commands finish. If
.B notify-send
is unavailable, prints a warning and preserves the main command result.
.TP
.BI "--specialisation " NAME
Build or activate a NixOS specialisation.
.TP
.BI "--target-host " HOST
Forward
.B --target-host
to
.BR nixos-rebuild .
.TP
.BI "--build-host " HOST
Forward
.B --build-host
to
.BR nixos-rebuild .
.TP
.B --use-remote-sudo
Forward
.B --use-remote-sudo
to
.BR nixos-rebuild .
.TP
.B --verbose
Print additional command context where supported.
.TP
.B --
Pass remaining arguments directly to the backend command.
.SH OUTPUT MODES
.TP
.B auto
Use
.B nom
for interactive lifecycle builds and plain output otherwise.
.TP
.B rich
Show a styled, bounded live derivation dependency graph plus summaries.
.TP
.B nom
Pipe build logs through
.BR "nom --json"
for an nh-like build tree. Requires
.BR nix-output-monitor .
.TP
.B plain
Print stable script-friendly summaries and warnings or errors only.
.TP
.B raw
Pass backend stdout and stderr through.
.TP
.B json
Print the final structured report as JSON.
.TP
.B jsonl
Print line-delimited lifecycle events.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Custom checks and hooks are argv arrays, not shell strings.
.PP
.EX
[hooks]
post_switch = [["systemctl", "--user", "restart", "waybar.service"]]

[ui]
# accent = "#cba6f7"
graph_depth = 12
refresh_ms = 500
verbose_backend = false

[state]
keep_logs = 20
keep_reports = 20
keep_history = 50
keep_plans = 10
.EE
.PP
.B post_activate
and
.B post_switch
hooks run only after successful activation. Their failures are reported as
warnings and do not turn the switch, test, boot, or apply result into a failure.
.PP
.B accent
sets the rich/nom UI accent color when configured. If unset, nr uses the
terminal's normal foreground color. It must be a six-digit hex color.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
.B --ui json
prints one final report object containing command, target, result, store_path,
current_generation, new_generation, reboot, rollback, log_path, build, diff,
and activation fields.
.PP
The diff object includes additions, removals, upgrades, downgrades, other
changes, important items, size_delta, and unavailable. The activation object
includes unit groups, caveats, and unavailable.
.SH ERROR MODEL
Build failures stop before activation and preserve the backend exit code.
Dry-activation failures are fatal for
.B switch
and
.BR test ,
but are reported as unavailable for
.BR preview .
Activation, pre-build, post-build, and pre-activate hook failures preserve the
failing command exit code. Post-activation hook failures are warnings after a
successful activation.
.SH LOGS
Default logs are written under
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/nr/logs/
or
.BR ~/.local/state/nr/logs/ .
.B nr
keeps the latest 20 default
.B nr-*.log
files by default. Reports, preview plans, and switch history are also bounded by
the
.B [state]
configuration. Explicit
.B --log-file
paths are never rotated.
.SH TARGET DISCOVERY
For commands that need a NixOS flake,
.B nr
checks these sources in order:
.IP "1." 4
.B --flake
.IP "2." 4
.B NR_FLAKE
.IP "3." 4
A
.B flake.nix
in the current directory or a parent directory
.IP "4." 4
.B [target].flake
in
.B ~/.config/nr/config.toml
.IP "5." 4
.B /etc/nixos
.PP
The host comes from
.BR --host ,
the
.B #HOST
flake fragment,
.BR NR_HOST ,
repo config, user config, or the machine hostname.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/nr/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.B .nr.toml
Repository configuration at the selected flake root.
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/nr/logs/
Default log directory when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/nr/pins.toml
Default generation pin file when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B nr preview --flake /etc/nixos#desktop
Build, diff, and dry-activate the
.B desktop
host without mutating system state.
.TP
.B nr switch --ask
Build, explain impact, ask for confirmation, then activate.
.TP
.B nr update nixpkgs --switch
Update one input, then build and activate after Git preflight.
.TP
.B nr diff --from 219 --to /nix/store/system-path
Diff generation 219 against a prebuilt system store path.
.TP
.B nr gc --dry-run
Preview collection of generations older than seven days.
.TP
.B nr pin 219 last-good
Label generation 219 as
.BR last-good .
.TP
.B nr build --ui raw --show-trace
Build with backend output passed through directly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B nr
exits with zero on success. Backend failures preserve the backend exit code
when it is available.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nixos-rebuild (8),
.BR nix (1),
.BR git (1)
